  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38154300",
      "title": "Solution: Analyze a Logfile",
      "lectureOrder": 74,
      "videoOrder": 53,
      "sourceHash": "fdaedde50945318d9122f3314780f97d3a0ff1d380e542f1ba8f51bff41eb56c",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 1.44,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.44,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at the solution about how we can analyze the log file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.25,
          "end": 11.24,
          "en": "So let's now have a look at how we can view that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.33,
          "end": 14.57,
          "en": "The easiest way would be, for example, with the head command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.57,
          "end": 19.72,
          "en": "And I could just say that I want to output, let's say the first four lines of my log file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.73,
          "end": 22.07,
          "en": "The log file is called access dot log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.07,
          "end": 25.07,
          "en": "So I can just output the first four lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.19,
          "end": 27.69,
          "en": "Then we can see that those lines are rather long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.71,
          "end": 29.24,
          "en": "This is why they wrap here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.84,
          "end": 31.76,
          "en": "So you can see this is the first line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.76,
          "end": 32.84,
          "en": "This is the second line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.84,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "This is the third line and the fourth line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.3,
          "end": 36.56,
          "en": "Let's look at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.56,
          "end": 42.23,
          "en": "And there, for example, I just use the tail command and we can see it continues kind of like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.23,
          "end": 47.81,
          "en": "So the whole file consists out of, um, of some logs and we can see some dates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.81,
          "end": 54.2,
          "en": "They were between 11th of July and 12th of July and the year is a little bit in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.2,
          "end": 56.21,
          "en": "Well, maybe a bit more but then a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.21,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "But we can see those files are log files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.68,
          "end": 62.24,
          "en": "What could be logged here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 65.78,
          "en": "Um, we can see here that there is an IP address here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.78,
          "end": 70.4,
          "en": "Sometimes it's IP version four, sometimes version six, IPV six.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.4,
          "end": 72.47,
          "en": "So we can see there's an IP address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.47,
          "end": 73.64,
          "en": "We got a date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.67,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "We got it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.53999999999999,
          "end": 77.51,
          "en": "This is could be a time zone offset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.53999999999999,
          "end": 79.61,
          "en": "This looks like a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.61,
          "end": 81.8,
          "en": "Maybe a file that was requested.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.01,
          "end": 83.03,
          "en": "Something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.03,
          "end": 85.19,
          "en": "There's something with Http here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.76,
          "end": 90.11,
          "en": "Um, which would be the protocol and the version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.23,
          "end": 98.09,
          "en": "1.1, there's this one here, but sometimes in this column there might also be a 404.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.09,
          "end": 100.67,
          "en": "Let's see if I output a few more lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.67,
          "end": 103.67,
          "en": "Let's say I output the last 40 lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.67,
          "end": 110.87,
          "en": "Then sometimes you might see a 302 we can find here and we can see here it's a little bit wrapped,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.87,
          "end": 113.24000000000001,
          "en": "but you can see it's 404.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.6,
          "end": 115.72999999999999,
          "en": "Um, that could not be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.72999999999999,
          "end": 121.85,
          "en": "So sometimes there's 404 um, here, which stands for that this file could not be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "Then we find a number here and then a URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.94,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "By the way, all those URL names are randomly generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "So if those exist, it's purely accidental.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.28,
          "end": 139.8,
          "en": "But we see there's like a domain or like a link here and then we can see something like this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.19,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "um, which is something, uh, it's somehow talking about Mozilla.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "Um, so something about the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 158.01,
          "en": "So to reveal what this log file is, this is the log file format from, for example, an Apache web",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 161.41,
          "en": "It's the so-called combined log file format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.43,
          "end": 163.86,
          "en": "You would not need to know that for the quiz.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 166.75,
          "en": "Um, but it's a log file of a web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 167.52,
          "en": "This is why you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.52,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "We have the IP of our of our visitor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.73,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "Uh, sometimes, uh, those IP addresses might be, um, randomized in a sense, for example, that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 182.62,
          "en": "the last few digits might be randomized in order to preserve privacy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 188.36,
          "en": "Then we have a date here we can see which has been requested from our server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 193.17,
          "en": "So for example, get would mean that we just want to request data post would mean that we would want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 193.17,
          "end": 195.93,
          "en": "to submit a form to our server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 198.9,
          "en": "Then this is the so-called response code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.9,
          "end": 201.77,
          "en": "Whether everything has worked or the file could not be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "So for example, 200 means everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 207.18,
          "en": "Okay, 404 means file could not be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "Then we have the so-called referrer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.55,
          "end": 211.62,
          "en": "This is where the user comes from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.62,
          "end": 216.66,
          "en": "So this website has sent the user to this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "Um, that would mean this referrer here again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 223.53,
          "en": "Again, they are all randomly generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 226.11,
          "en": "So if they do exist is pure accident.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 234.39,
          "en": "Just try not to click on them and not open them because again, it's completely random, the domain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then you can see here the so called user agents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "This is what the browser tells our server, what he is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 241.47,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "And in this case I've checked that actually it's quite an old system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "It's a Chrome 96 on Windows 8.1, the corresponding user agent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 251.07,
          "end": 256.47,
          "en": "It's putting this Mozilla here because Firefox once was a really popular browser and back in the days",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 256.47,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "they wanted the server to enable the more advanced features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 266.85,
          "en": "So that's why Mozilla is here, even though it's not a Mozilla and it's also adding this one for servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 273.69,
          "en": "Um that that might check for that one but at the end it's a chrome 96 at least it looks like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 273.69,
          "end": 278.58,
          "en": "Um, it's sometimes a little bit difficult to parse those uh, user agents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 279.03,
          "end": 285.61,
          "en": "Um, but you can see that this is a log file from a web server and all the requests here have been logged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 285.85,
          "end": 289.12,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at how we can analyze that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 289.12,
          "end": 296.59000000000003,
          "en": "So for example, one thing that we were interested where the number of lines so I can say um, w C minus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 296.59000000000003,
          "end": 300.73,
          "en": "L access dot log and we can see it's 10,000 lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 300.73,
          "end": 305.59,
          "en": "This is because I've generated and I was like, okay, I'll just generate 10,000 lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 305.98,
          "end": 310.84,
          "en": "The next thing was the file size that we were interested in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 310.87,
          "end": 313.69,
          "en": "That was the Du disk usage command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 313.69,
          "end": 318.88,
          "en": "But I'm here on the Mac and it doesn't really display, uh, it's a little bit weird how it displays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 318.88,
          "end": 319.69,
          "en": "that one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 319.69,
          "end": 325.93,
          "en": "So the way to go is that I need the minus H flag here for my disk usage and then we can see that the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 325.93,
          "end": 329.59,
          "en": "file is three megabytes in size or about three megabytes in size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 329.8,
          "end": 334.51,
          "en": "So this is how you can solve this problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 334.51,
          "end": 342.78,
          "en": "And you have seen that we are we were able to display the log file without outputting all of them and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 342.78,
          "end": 348.72,
          "en": "this would be more efficient, especially imagine the file would be like 300 or 3000MB in size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 349.05,
          "end": 349.68,
          "en": "All right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 349.68,
          "end": 352.5,
          "en": "This is how you could have solved this exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
